 ## The MemoryProvider ABC
+
+### Host-owned LLM access
+
+The provider registration context exposes `ctx.llm` just like ordinary plugins,
+including when the provider runs in the plugin host subprocess. Persistent
+providers should retain `ctx.bound_llm` instead: this facade rejects another
+profile's ambient home, checks live auxiliary-task ownership on every call and
+is revoked on plugin unload. It supports the same four completion methods.
+
+After `ctx.register_auxiliary_task(...)`, call
+`ctx.bound_llm.binding(task="your_task")`. Its serializable result contains
+`contract_version=1`, `plugin_id`, `profile_home`, `task` and `task_registered`.
+Compare `profile_home` with the `hermes_home` passed to `initialize`, require the
+expected plugin ID and `task_registered is True`, and repeat the check before
+background extraction. A registration method returning without an exception is
+not proof that the task registered: secondary provider registrations may fail
+without costing the memory provider itself. These metadata never contain keys.
+
+The facade is an instance-local runtime capability; do not serialize it into a
+database or share it through a process-global singleton. Reacquire it through
+`register` after restart. This contract does not grant filesystem isolation,
+gateway admission, or permission to send private conversation text to a model.
+
+Providers that resolve gateway identity use `ctx.bound_session.snapshot()` rather
+than reading child-process ContextVars. It reads the parent caller's live
+`platform`, `chat_id`, `chat_type`, `user_id`, `thread_id`, `session_id`, and
+`message_id` as strings. Unset values are empty, with no environment fallback.
+`binding()` returns `contract_version=1`, `plugin_id`, and `profile_home`; verify
+these at initialization. This facade has the same profile and unload boundaries
+as `bound_llm`. It never caches identity or accepts user/model identity fields.
+Detached hosted work has no active caller and gets empty fields; durable jobs
+must use their persisted, re-authorized scope rather than a previous snapshot.
 
